---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { HISTOIRES } from '../../moteur/chapitres';
---
<Base
  titre="Sysadmin Quests"
  langue="en"
  autre={{ href: '/', langue: 'fr', nom: 'Français' }}
  description="Learn Linux system administration by playing, in your browser, with real commands: moving around, searching, permissions, logs, networking, git, backups."
>
  <h1>Sysadmin Quests</h1>
  <p class="intro">
    Adventures where you act with <strong>real Linux commands</strong>. Every place is a
    directory, every object a file. {HISTOIRES.length} independent stories: start with The Eraser
    if you have never opened a terminal.
  </p>
  <p class="intro">
    Stuck? Do as the pros do: <code>man command</code> opens the manual,
    <code>command --help</code> gives a summary, and <code>man -k word</code> finds the command
    that does what you want.
  </p>
  <p class="intro">
    The game was written in French and translated into English. For now, the files and places
    of the game world keep their French names (you type them as they are; the texts explain
    them): <code>cd Phare</code>, <code>cat courriel_kofi.txt</code>.
  </p>
  <noscript><p class="avertissement">This game needs JavaScript to simulate a terminal in your browser.</p></noscript>

  <quetes-de-sysadmin langue="en"></quetes-de-sysadmin>

  <section aria-labelledby="embed">
    <h2 id="embed">Put the game on your site</h2>
    <p>The game is free software and fits in any page with two lines:</p>
    <pre><code>{`<script type="module" src="https://sysadmin.rouages.net/integration/quetes-de-sysadmin.js"></script>
<quetes-de-sysadmin langue="en"></quetes-de-sysadmin>`}</code></pre>
    <p>Full instructions (in French): <a href="https://github.com/Rouages-du-net/quetes-de-sysadmin/blob/main/docs/INTEGRER.md" hreflang="fr">docs/INTEGRER.md</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  import '../../element';
</script>
